99cd4e from an earlier instance was run on this test input first, and its output was submitted:\n```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    from collections import Counter\n    R, W = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    c = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row)\n    accent = min(c, key=c.get)\n    has = [any(v == accent for v in row) for row in grid]\n    bands = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < R:\n        if has[i]:\n            j = i\n            while j + 1 < R and has[j + 1]:\n                j += 1\n            bands.append((i, j))\n            i = j + 1\n        else:\n            i += 1\n    out = [list(row) for row in grid]\n\n    def cols_of(r):\n        return [k for k, v in enumerate(grid[r]) if v == accent]\n\n    def prefix_row(r):\n        cs = cols_of(r)\n        return cs[0] == 0 and all(cs[k + 1] == cs[k] + 1 for k in range(len(cs) - 1))\n\n    if all(j0 - i0 == 0 for i0, j0 in bands):\n        for i0, j0 in bands:\n            r = i0\n            if prefix_row(r):\n                last = cols_of(r)[-1]\n                for j in range(last + 1, W):\n                    out[r][j] = 1\n        return out\n\n    def src_ext(srow, sc):\n        if 0 <= sc < W:\n            return srow[sc]\n        return srow[W - 2 + (sc - W) % 2]\n\n    for bi in range(1, len(bands)):\n        i0, j0 = bands[bi]\n        pi, pj = bands[bi - 1]\n        for idx, r in enumerate(range(i0, j0 + 1)):\n            src = pi + idx\n            if src > pj:\n                src = pj\n            srow = grid[src]\n            last = cols_of(r)[-1]\n            for j in range(last + 1, W):\n                if src_ext(srow, j + 1) == accent:\n                    out[r][j] = 1\n    return out\n```\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-dc99cd4e\nTest input (23x17):\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 3 3 7 3 7 3 7\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 3 7 3 7 3 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 3 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7\n3 3 3 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7\n7 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3 7 3\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\nWrong attempts used: 1/8. Demo requests used: 0/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"Looking at this task across all demonstration pairs, I derived a unified rule:\n\n- **When full-width accent rows exist** (pairs 1,2,3,5,6,7): they act as templates; every background cell in partial accent rows becomes 1 (the bar is completed to the pattern's full extent).\n- **When no full rows exist** (pair 4): the two accent bands are copies of the same pattern under a horizontal shift. The band with fewer accent cells is an incomplete copy — its background cells where the other band (shifted) implies accent become 1.\n\nVerifying pair 4: bottom band = top band shifted right by 2, truncated; fills at exactly (r10: 14,15,17,18,20), (r12: 16,19) ✓.\n\nFor the test input: bands at rows 5–8 (21 accents) and 18–21 (26 accents). Best alignment is shift −8 (band2 = band1 shifted left 8: r19 = r6−8 exactly, r18/r20/r21 = virtual extensions of r5/r7/r8 minus 8). The smaller band (top) is incomplete: implied accents from band2 shifted +8 give r8 needing accent at column 16 (r21's 16 = 24−8). Exactly one violation: cell (8,16) → 1. Every other implied accent is already present.\n\n```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    from collections import Counter\n    R = len(grid); W = len(grid[0])\n    out = [list(row) for row in grid]\n    cnt = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row)\n    if len(cnt) < 2:\n        return out\n    accent = min(cnt, key=lambda c: (cnt[c], c))\n    A = [[c for c, v in enumerate(row) if v == accent] for row in grid]\n    arows = [r for r in range(R) if A[r]]\n    if not arows:\n        return out\n    full = [r for r in arows if len(A[r]) == W]\n    if full:\n        for r in arows:\n            if len(A[r]) < W:\n                for c in range(W):\n                    if grid[r][c] != accent:\n                        out[r][c] = 1\n        return out\n    bands = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < R:\n        if A[i]:\n            j = i\n            while j + 1 < R and A[j + 1]:\n                j += 1\n            bands.append((i, j))\n            i = j + 1\n        else:\n            i += 1\n    for (i1, j1), (i2, j2) in zip(bands, bands[1:]):\n        n = min(j1 - i1, j2 - i2) + 1\n        A1 = [set(A[i1 + k]) for k in range(n)]\n        A2 = [set(A[i2 + k]) for k in range(n)]\n        best = None\n        for s in range(-(W - 1), W):\n            sc = 0\n            for k in range(n):\n                sh = {a + s for a in A1[k]}\n                sc += len(A2[k] & sh)\n            if best is None or sc > best[0] or (sc == best[0] and abs(s) < abs(best[1])):\n                best = (sc, s)\n        s = best[1]\n        c1 = sum(len(x) for x in A1)\n        c2 = sum(len(x) for x in A2)\n        if c2 <= c1:\n            for k in range(n):\n                for c in range(W):\n                    if grid[i2 + k][c] != accent and (c - s) in A1[k]:\n                        out[i2 + k][c] = 1\n        else:\n            for k in range(n):\n                for c in range(W):\n                    if grid[i1 + k][c] != accent and (c + s) in A2[k]:\n                        out[i1 + k][c] = 1\n    return out\n```\n\nThis reproduces all 7 demonstration pairs and yields the test output = input with grid[8][16] set to 1.\n\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":true}}]}